Well, this is my first ascension. Unfortunately, it wasn't on a public
server, so no playback/whatever.

Anyway: the details: Val-Dwa-Fem-Law, artiwishless, polypileless.

I started out much worse than the previous game, which had been lost
to YASD by electric eel drowning on Medusa's level. Minetown was a
bones level with a dead coaligned priest and a previous reincarnation
of myself. So I went to do the valkyrie quest, fell into lava twice,
found a bag of holding, which i threw away in anger because sokoban
had already had one.
I ended up at Medusa's level with uncontrolled teleportitis, no
reflection, no MR, no conflict, and blanked and rusty loot, because i
kept stupidly falling into water. The only thing that had allowed me
to get thus far was the +7 Excalibur and the Orb of Fate. I also found
Mjollnir... in the main dungeon, randomly generated. So there goes any
chance of the sceptre for conflict and MR. Not wanting to
inadvertently teleport straight into Medusa, I dug down for the castle
(yes, without reflection and MR) and used the drawbridge to clear most
of it out. I made it to the wand of wishing, went for 2 blessed
scrolls of charging (got 1), blessed +2 SDSM (got +0), and returned to
find that my pet large cat had gone feral on me, and I killed it
before I realized that it was my old pet. The castle throne gave me a
genocide, at which I promptly genocided master mind flayers. As soon
as I entered the Valley of the Dead... bam, mind flayer sucks me,
which conveniently causes me to forget what genocide scrolls look
like. Gehennom was relatively uneventful, and I wished for cloak of
MR, and ring of teleport control, because i had found a random wand of
wishing from a death drop. I burned my amulet of life saving from
Vlad's tower by accident, not noticing that Rodney had stolen the Orb,
on which i was relying to give me half physical damage. The mysterious
force was nice to me, and I walked up to Dlvl 1, wished for food
detection, wrote 3 more, and prepared for the elemental planes. from
then on, i reserved a wand of death for rodney.

All 4 planes were easy, but I was completely unprepared for Astral. I
took some advice and used telepathy to find famine and go for that
altar first using my wands of teleportation. oops, wrong altar. Then I
ran for the one guarded by death, which was also wrong. At this point,
I wished for another amulet of life saving. absolutely stupid
decision. much better would have been a ring of conflict... so i ended
up wishing for 3, as 1 after another monster killed me trying to get
back from the second altar. at this point, with 3 HP but wearing an
amulet, I wished for conflict, put it on with my spare turn from speed
potion (i forgot to mention that i was jumping around with my boots
and my magic lamp), and managed to quaff my full healing potion while
everything else was hitting each other. this made it much easier, and
I strolled around pestilence, walked over to the altar, grabbed 2 bits
for a celestial ale from the high priest, and ascended.

